  "id": "emic",
  "term": "emic",
  "definition": "Emic refers to an approach that studies behavior or practices from within a particular culture, emphasizing how local social and cultural meanings shape them. In psychology and related social research, it means understanding a topic in the terms of the people and setting being studied rather than treating it as the same across cultures.",
